@{include("./Commons/header-common.i")}

  <link rel='canonical' href='@{siteAddress}/'>
  <title>Michael Heilmann's Project Arcadia</title>

  <meta property="og:title" content="Michael Heilmann's Project Arcadia">
  <meta property="og:description" content="Arcadia is an open environment for creating, regenerating, and preserving games. A game is a set of clear, editable text documents rather than a binary, so it can be read, shared, regenerated, and kept long after its engine is gone.">
  <meta name="description" content="Arcadia is an open environment for creating, regenerating, and preserving games. A game is a set of clear, editable text documents rather than a binary, so it can be read, shared, regenerated, and kept long after its engine is gone.">
  <meta name="keywords" content="Arcadia, Game Development, Procedural Generation, Audials, Visuals, Open Source, Free Software">
  <meta name="author" content="@{siteAuthor}">
</head>
<body class="my-index-page-1">
  <header>
    <div class="banner left-column">
      <div>Michael Heilmann's</div>
      <h1>Project Arcadia</h1>
    </div>
    <div class="center-column"></div>
    <div class="right-column">
      <nav>
        <ul style="display: flex; flex-direction: row; gap: 1rem;">
          <li><a href="@{siteAddress}/Arcadia/">Documentation</a></li>
          <li><a href="@{siteAddress}/building">Building</a></li>
          <li><a href='@{arcadiaGitHubAddress}'>GitHub</a></li>
          <li><a href='https://discord.gg/XtPA6pwAsp'>Discord</a></li>
        </ul>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </header>
  <main>
    <div class="topic left-column">
      <div class="header">
        <span>The idea</span>
      </div>
      <div class="body">
        <p><em>A game is a set of text documents, not a binary.</em></p>

        <p>Those documents describe the game's visuals, audials, and logics in plain, editable prose and markup, and
        Arcadia regenerates the whole game from them whenever it is needed. Nothing is lost that only a compiler or a
        level editor ever knew.</p>

        <p>What that leaves you with is something you can read, diff, share, and hand to the next person. Not just
        something you can run.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="topic center-column">
      <div class="header">
        <span>What that buys you</span>
      </div>
      <div class="body">
        <p><em>Portable</em> &mdash; the descriptions carry no platform assumptions, so a game travels to another
        platform without being rewritten for it.</p>

        <p><em>Regenerable</em> &mdash; deterministic procedural generation rebuilds rich worlds, sounds, and
        behaviour from compact text.</p>

        <p><em>Preservable</em> &mdash; the description is the artifact. It outlives the engine, the platform, and
        often the person who wrote it.</p>

        <p><em>Self-publishing</em> &mdash; Arcadia emits each game as a complete, self-contained website, ready for
        a static host or for reading offline.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="topic right-column">
      <div class="header">
        <span>Where to go</span>
      </div>
      <div class="body">
        <div class="entries">
          <a href='@{siteAddress}/Arcadia/'>Documentation</a>
          <a href='@{siteAddress}/building'>Building Arcadia</a>
          <a href='@{siteAddress}/Arcadia/roadmap'>Roadmap</a>
          <a href='@{arcadiaGitHubAddress}'>Arcadia GitHub repository</a>
          <a href='https://discord.gg/XtPA6pwAsp'>Discord server</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
  <!--
    A one-line teaser for each of the three most recent news entries.
    The dates are the fragment file names, which are the source of truth;
    the full entries are listed in Arcadia/news.html.te.
  -->
  <div class="news-band">
    <h2>News</h2>
    <ul class="news-latest">
      <li>
        <a href="@{siteAddress}/Arcadia/news">2026-09-29</a>
        <span>The PDL specification and the consolidated PDLC compiler, the ADL
        documentation, Arcadia.Engine.Text, and Ring 1 interface types.</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="@{siteAddress}/Arcadia/news">2026-03-30</a>
        <span>A consistent pattern in Ring 1 and Ring 2 for reading bytes and
        decoding them to code points.</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="@{siteAddress}/Arcadia/news">2026-03-07</a>
        <span>Engine.Visuals and Engine.Audials merge into Arcadia Engine,
        buffers consolidate into Arcadia Media, and ADL gains declarative
        asset descriptions.</span>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  @{include("./footer.i")}
</body>
</html>
